Sil-Q, packaged for the Asciiverse.

Sil-Q is the maintained continuation of Sil, the roguelike of the First
Age of Middle-earth by half and Scatha (Sil 1.0 in 2012, Sil 1.3 in 2016,
http://www.amirrorclear.net/flowers/game/sil/). Quirk started Sil-Q from
the Sil 1.3 code in 2017 and led it to 1.5.0 in 2022, with tiles and the
manual by MicroChasm; Michael G. Noll carries it on today at
https://github.com/sil-quirk/sil-q with the Sil-Q community. Sil itself grew
from NPPAngband and Angband (Ben Harrison, James E. Wilson, Robert A.
Koeneke and many others).

Licence: LICENSE.md, beside this file, lets you use Sil-Q under either
the GNU General Public License, version 2, or the Angband licence. The
Asciiverse distributes it under the GNU General Public License,
version 2. The complete source of this build, with every change the
Asciiverse made listed in PATCHES.md, is at
https://github.com/theasciiverse/sil-q.

This archive holds only the terminal (curses) build. Sil-Q's sounds are
left out: LICENSE.md calls them only "freeware, whatever that means",
and the terminal build plays none. The tiles and fonts, which it does
not use either, are left out too.

Saved characters, high scores, pref files and character dumps are kept
in your data folder, $XDG_DATA_HOME/sil-q, or ~/.local/share/sil-q.
